# Voyago Mobile — environment configuration
#
# Expo CLI automatically loads EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables from .env files and
# inlines them into the JS bundle at build time. They are NOT secret —
# Firebase's security model relies on Firestore/Auth rules, not on hiding
# these values. See https://firebase.google.com/docs/projects/api-keys
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (already gitignored via the .env*.local
# pattern) and fill in the real values from the existing Voyago Firebase
# project (ask a teammate, or Firebase Console -> Project settings ->
# General -> Your apps -> web app "voyago-7c088").
#
# NEVER add any of the following to this app, in any form, under any
# variable name:
#   FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY, FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL  — Firebase Admin SDK
#     service-account credentials. Server-only, live in the website repo's
#     Netlify Functions environment.
#   CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET, CLOUDINARY_API_KEY    — Cloudinary signing
#     credentials. Server-only, same reason.
# A client app (web or mobile) that ships any of these could let anyone who
# decompiles the app bypass Firestore rules entirely or forge Cloudinary
# uploads/deletes.

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-api-key
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:0000000000000000000000
